    <summary>Multi-terminal host for Claude Code and other CLI coding agents on Windows.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
**CodeShellManager** is a desktop app for running many AI coding agents side by side: Claude Code, Codex, GitHub Copilot, or any CLI tool, in one window of terminal panes over Windows ConPTY.

Version 2 is a rewrite in Rust. It upgrades an installed CodeShellManager 0.x in place and, on first start, brings over its sessions (asleep), groups and project notes; the old data folder is left untouched.

## Features

* Many terminal sessions in tiled, side-by-side and floating layouts, grouped by project
* Sleep and wake: park sessions without losing them; sessions are restored on start
* Full-text search across session output, per-project notes, git status and worktrees
* Alerts when a session needs you, as Windows notifications and in the tray
* The `csm` command-line tool and an MCP server (`csm mcp`) that let agents drive the app
* WSL and SSH sessions, configurable launch commands, Open with

## Requirements

* Windows 10 or Windows 11, x64

## License

CodeShellManager is open source under the [MIT License](https://github.com/umage-ai/CodeShellManager/blob/main/LICENSE).
]]></description>
